Vendor Tarball
==============

Cloud Hypervisor is packaged with a vendored Rust dependencies tarball
(orig-vendor.tar.xz) since building requires network access to fetch
crates, which is not available during package builds.

Regenerating the vendor tarball
-------------------------------

From a clean upstream source tree at the desired release tag:

    cargo vendor vendor/

Then create the tarball:

    UPSTREAM_VERSION=<version>
    tar --sort=name --mtime="@0" --owner=root --group=root \
        -cJf ../cloud-hypervisor_${UPSTREAM_VERSION}+ds1.orig-vendor.tar.xz vendor/

The +dsN suffix
---------------

The "+ds1" suffix in the version string indicates the first Debian Source
modification — in this case the addition of the vendor tarball which is not
part of the upstream release artefact. If the vendor tarball needs to be
regenerated independently of a new upstream release (e.g. to add or update
a dependency), bump the suffix to +ds2, +ds3, etc.

The upstream orig tarball (without vendor/) keeps its plain version:

    cloud-hypervisor_<version>.orig.tar.xz

Generating debian/copyright
----------------------------

The debian/copyright file is generated from the vendored crates metadata
using:

    debian/gen-copyright.py > debian/copyright

This script parses each vendor/<crate>/Cargo.toml for license and author
information and produces a DEP-5 machine-readable copyright file. It also
includes per-file overrides for cases where individual source files carry
a different license than the crate-level Cargo.toml declares (e.g.
auto-generated bindings with BSD headers).

After regenerating the vendor tarball, always re-run the script and review
the diff to catch any new or changed licenses.
